TASK 1 – GUI DESIGN REVIEW
Student Fee Payment Window – 6 Marks
Task 1.1 – Diagnose the Design (2 Marks)
The given program has several design problems:
No.	Design deficiency	What could go wrong?
1	Poor separation of interface and logic	GUI code directly performs database operations. Testing and maintenance become difficult.
2	Incorrect string comparison using ==	String values should be compared using .equals(). The Pay action may not be identified correctly.
3	No input validation	Empty registration numbers, negative amounts, or letters may cause errors.
4	Database work on the event-dispatch thread	The window may freeze while the database operation is running.
5	Use of Thread.sleep(3000)	The GUI becomes unresponsive for three seconds.
6	No proper user feedback	The user may not know whether the payment succeeded or failed.
7	Receipt button is not implemented	Clicking Receipt does not display a payment receipt.
8	SQL statement uses string concatenation	It can cause SQL injection and errors when input contains special characters.
9	Database connection is not closed	It may cause resource leaks and eventually prevent new connections.
10	No exception handling	Database errors and checked exceptions may terminate the operation unexpectedly.
11	No proper window-closing operation	The application may not close cleanly.

Task 1.2 – Repair the Design (3 Marks)
1. Proposed design
The redesigned application separates the GUI from the payment logic.
- FeeWindow: Collects registration number and amount, displays messages, and handles button clicks.
- FeeService: Validates input and performs the database payment operation.
- SwingWorker: Runs database work in the background so the GUI does not freeze.
- Payment receipt: Stores and displays the details of the successful payment.
